- Exception isolation preserved: W3/W4 sit in the existing never-lose-wave-1/2-codes guard,
  W4 nested so its failure cannot lose W3's code. Announced sleep ("sleeping 10s for WAVE-3
  to work") keeps the daily review's gap classifier clean.

## Why
The old wave 3 was believed to be a plain working limit at 1.70 (chat "Hacker script max
spread price", and the hacker backtest models fill-at-cross up to the cap), but as coded it
was a Seeker quoting at surface+ET2 with 1.70 only as an outer bound -- more passive than the
validated model exactly on fast-market days. 9/9 evidence: wave-3 fills at 1.00-1.10 vs
quotes it could have crossed; the model/prod gap surfaced as "attempted but never filled,
delta_pnl 0" lines.

